# Web: landing-page heroes

Public marketing pages pair **breadcrumbs** and **gradient hero titles** inside the hero band. Reference heroes: `PublicMcpHero.svelte`, `PublicAgentHero.svelte`, `PublicChannelHero.svelte`, `PublicApiMarketingHero.svelte`, and every `*ToolPage.svelte` under `/tools`.

## Hero title styling (`*Hero.svelte`)

Never render `{heroTitle}` as plain text in an `<h1>`. Use `PublicLandingHeroTitle.svelte` (or the same `landingHeroTheme` segment loop) so copy picks up gradient spans and `LandingHeroHighlightedText` chips.

```svelte
<PublicLandingHeroTitle title={heroVm.heroTitle} headingId="my-hero-heading" />
```

| Piece | Path |
| --- | --- |
| Theme + highlight dictionary | `web/src/lib/ui/templates/landing-page/landingHeroTheme.ts` |
| Shared `<h1>` renderer | `PublicLandingHeroTitle.svelte` |
| Highlight chip wrapper | `LandingHeroHighlightedText.svelte` |

When `heroTitle` introduces new product names or phrases that should pop, append them to `LANDING_HERO_TITLE_HIGHLIGHT_WORDS` in `landingHeroTheme.ts` (**longest phrases first**). Match the exact wording used in the constant/`heroTitle` string (case-insensitive). See **add-agent** for agent/MCP labels.

Optional `heroTheme` prop on `PublicLandingHeroTitle` when a page passes a custom theme object (defaults to `landingHeroTheme`).

