# Web: landing-page breadcrumbs

Public marketing heroes use a **breadcrumb trail** in place of the old uppercase eyebrow/subtitle (e.g. `Scheduling API`, `MCP`, platform label alone). Trails are **centered above the `<h1>`** inside the hero band — same vertical slot as the previous subtitle.

## Shared building blocks

| Piece | Path |
| --- | --- |
| Hub labels (Title Case source strings) | `web/src/lib/content/constants/publicLandingBreadcrumbConfig.ts` |
| Link/page/separator classes | `web/src/lib/ui/templates/landing-page/publicLandingBreadcrumbStyles.ts` |
| Generic renderer (`items[]`) | `PublicLandingHubBreadcrumb.svelte` |
| DaisyUI breadcrumb primitives | `$lib/ui/breadcrumb` |

**Styling:** marketing and tool breadcrumbs render **uppercase** via `PUBLIC_LANDING_BREADCRUMB_*_CLASS` in `publicLandingBreadcrumbStyles.ts` — store labels in Title Case in markup/constants; do not hand-type ALL CAPS.

**Blog exception:** `BlogHubBreadcrumb.svelte` uses `PUBLIC_BLOG_BREADCRUMB_*_CLASS` (no `uppercase`) so the hub link reads **Blog**, not **BLOG**. Post/topic/author titles stay Title Case on the current segment.

**Links:** use `hostedMarketingHref(..., page.url.origin)` and `route(getRootPath…())` helpers — not raw paths (**web-hosted-marketing-links**).

## Component naming

Add route-specific breadcrumb components under `web/src/lib/ui/templates/landing-page/` (or the matching template folder, e.g. `api-marketing/`):

- `PublicAgentsLandingBreadcrumb.svelte`
- `PublicChannelsLandingBreadcrumb.svelte`
- `PublicApiMarketingHubBreadcrumb.svelte`
- `HumanizeHubBreadcrumb.svelte`, `PhotoEditorHubBreadcrumb.svelte`, `SkillBuilderHubBreadcrumb.svelte`, `BestTimeToPostHubBreadcrumb.svelte`, `PayloadWizardHubBreadcrumb.svelte`

Each wrapper builds an `items` array and delegates to `PublicLandingHubBreadcrumb`. Wire breadcrumbs **into the hero template**, not a separate container above the hero.

## Route trails

| Route | Breadcrumb |
| --- | --- |
| `/agents` | **Home** → Agents |
| `/agents/{slug}` (MCP client) | **Home** → MCP Integrations → `{agentLabel}` (MCP Integrations links to `/agents#public-mcp-hub-heading`) |
| `/agents/{slug}` (agent host) | **Home** → Autonomous Agent Integrations → `{agentLabel}` (hub segment links to `/agents#public-autonomous-agent-hub-heading`) |
| `/agents/{slug}/{channelSlug}` | Same as slug row, plus → `{channelLabel}` (agent/MCP segment links back to `/agents/{slug}`) |
| `/channels` | **Supported Channels** (current page only — no Home) |
| `/channels/{slug}` | **Supported Channels** → `{platformLabel}` |
| `/social-media-posting-api` | **Home** → Social Media Posting API |
| `/social-media-posting-api/{slug}` | **Home** → Social Media Posting API → `{platformLabel}` |
| `/social-media-scheduling-api` | **Home** → Social Media Scheduling API |
| `/social-media-scheduling-api/{slug}` | **Home** → Social Media Scheduling API → `{platformLabel}` |
| `/tools` | **Free Tools** (breadcrumb on tool pages; hub uses eyebrow + `PublicLandingHeroTitle`) |
| `/tools/humanizer` (+ `{channelSlug}`) | **Free Tools** → Humanizer [→ `{channelLabel}`] |
| `/tools/photo-editor`, `/tools/skill-builder`, `/tools/best-time-to-post`, `/tools/payload-wizard` | Same pattern: **Free Tools** → tool name [→ channel] |

Hub labels for agents/channels come from `PUBLIC_LANDING_BREADCRUMB` in `publicLandingBreadcrumbConfig.ts`. Scroll targets for the two `/agents` integration sections live in `PUBLIC_AGENTS_HUB_SECTION_IDS` (must match `headingId` on `PublicAgentsHubGrid` / `PublicMcpHubGrid`). API marketing hub titles come from `metaTitle` in the posting/scheduling hub VM.

## Hero integration checklist

When adding or changing a public landing hero:

1. **Remove** the standalone eyebrow `<p>` (platform label, `MCP`, `Agents`, etc.) from the hero.
2. **Render** the matching `*Breadcrumb.svelte` in a centered wrapper (`flex justify-center`) immediately above the title.
3. **Coming-soon heroes** (`PublicComingSoonIntegrationPage`) — use the same breadcrumb component; pass agent/MCP variant props when the page is under `/agents/...`.
4. **Hub grids** — pass a `{#snippet breadcrumb()}` into `FeaturesSectionHeader` when that header owns the page `<h1>`, or inline the breadcrumb where the hub subtitle used to live (`PublicChannelsHubGrid`).
5. **Channel/agent depth** — pass `activeChannelLabel` / `channelLabel` from the route into the landing template so slug and channel-slug pages share one hero.
6. **Hero title** — render `heroTitle` through `PublicLandingHeroTitle` (see **Hero title styling** above); extend `LANDING_HERO_TITLE_HIGHLIGHT_WORDS` when new phrases need highlight chips.

## Tool SEO titles (`/tools/*`)

Programmatic copy lives in `web/src/lib/content/utils/buildProgrammaticSeoTitles.ts`. Follow the PostPeer-style split used across free tools:

| Field | Purpose | Pattern |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `metaTitle` | SERP `<title>` (brand appended in `+page.server.ts`) | `Free {Tool or Platform descriptor} — No Sign Up` (Payload Wizard uses `— Copy POST /public/posts JSON` instead) |
| `heroTitle` | On-page `<h1>` via `PublicLandingHeroTitle` | `Free {platform?} {tool name}` — reader-facing, usually lowercase after "Free" |
| `metaDescription` | Meta + JSON-LD | Lead with "Free … in your browser" and end with "No sign up required" when the tool is guest-usable |

- **Channel slugs** (`/tools/{tool}/{channelSlug}`) — builders take `platformLabel` from `publicChannelConfig` (e.g. `Free YouTube photo editor` H1, `Free YouTube Photo Editor — No Sign Up` title).
- **Do not** reuse `metaTitle` as the visible H1 on tool pages — always pass `heroTitle` into the hero template.
- **JSON-LD** `name` stays on `metaTitle` (keyword target), not `heroTitle`.

## API marketing hero titles (`/social-media-*-api`)

Follow [PostPeer](https://www.postpeer.dev/social-media-posting-api)-style keyword H1s — value props belong in `heroDescription`, not the title:

| Route | `heroTitle` |
| --- | --- |
| Posting hub | `Social Media Posting API` |
| Scheduling hub | `Social Media Scheduling API` |
| Platform slug | `{PlatformLabel} Posting API` / `{PlatformLabel} Scheduling API` (override label with `heroPlatformLabel`, e.g. `Twitter / X`) |

Builders: `buildPublicApiHubHeroTitle`, `buildPublicApiPlatformHeroTitle` in `buildProgrammaticSeoTitles.ts`. Platform pages default the H1 in `buildPublicApiPlatformPage()` when `heroTitle` is omitted.

In `LANDING_HERO_TITLE_HIGHLIGHT_WORDS`, chip suffix terms only (`Posting API`, `Scheduling API`, `Twitter / X`) — never the full hub H1 (`Social Media Posting API`) or the entire title becomes one white highlight tile.

## API marketing audience section (`WhoIsFor`)

Hub and platform pages render `PublicApiMarketingWhoIsFor.svelte` **directly below** `PublicApiMarketingHero`, then `PublicApiMarketingHubSetupSteps.svelte` (platform slugs pass `platformLabel` for tailored step copy), then payload validator / format sections. Copy: `publicApiCapabilityAudienceConfig.ts` — three cards (SaaS developers, Vibe coders, Startup teams) with posting vs scheduling variants; platform slugs append a `{platformLabel}` hook.

**Schema.org:** `WhoIsFor.svelte` is presentational only. Page loaders emit JSON-LD via `createPublicAudienceSEOSchema.ts`:

- **`ItemList`** at `{canonical}#audience` — one `ListItem` per card with `BusinessAudience` / `PeopleAudience` on `item`
- **`audience`** on `SoftwareApplication`, `WebPage`, or `CollectionPage` — same persona nodes linked to the product/page

Helper: `createPublicAudienceSectionSEOSchema`, `withSchemaOrgAudience`, `buildSchemaOrgAudienceFromCards`. Home cards live in `publicLandingWhoIsForConfig.ts`.

## Setup steps section (`FeaturesOrdered`)

Agent, MCP, and API marketing pages render ordered setup steps via `FeaturesOrdered.svelte` (or wrappers `PublicApiMarketingHubSetupSteps.svelte`). Copy lives in agent/MCP VMs (`setupSteps*`) or `publicApiCapabilityHubSetupStepsConfig.ts`. Section footers (`New to OpenQuok?` + docs link) resolve from `publicSetupStepsFooterConfig.ts` — API → `/docs/getting-started-for-public-api`, agents → `docsPath`, MCP client tab → `docsPath`, MCP skill tab → `/docs/getting-started-for-cli`.

**Schema.org:** `FeaturesOrdered.svelte` is presentational only. Page loaders emit **`HowTo`** JSON-LD via `createPublicSetupStepsSEOSchema.ts` at `{canonical}#setup-steps`. MCP pages also emit `#skill-setup-steps` for the skill tab (`buildPublicMcpSetupStepsSeoSchemas`). Pass optional `sectionId` on `FeaturesOrdered` so the visible section `id` matches the JSON-LD fragment. Do not use `ItemList` alone for procedural steps — [`HowTo`](https://schema.org/HowTo) + [`HowToStep`](https://schema.org/HowToStep) match the section semantics. Optional step media (`terminalCode`, device mocks) stays out of JSON-LD; only plain `title` and `content` are included.

## API marketing pricing section (`PublicMarketingPricingSection`)

Hub and platform API pages render **`PublicMarketingPricingSection.svelte`** **after** feature rows and **before** FAQ. Home (`LandingPage.svelte`) uses the same wrapper with `presetId="home"` and optional CMS overlay.

**Section order (API marketing hub + platform slugs):**

1. `PublicApiMarketingHero`
2. `PublicApiMarketingWhoIsFor`
3. `PublicApiMarketingHubSetupSteps` (platform slugs pass `platformLabel`)
4. Payload validator / format sections (`PublicApiMarketingPayloadValidatorSection`, `PublicApiMarketingStaticExampleBento`, platform format bento when present)
5. Hub or sibling grid (`PublicApiMarketingHubGrid` / `PublicApiMarketingSiblingGrid`)
6. `PublicApiMarketingFeatureRows`
7. **`PublicMarketingPricingSection`**
8. `PublicFaq`

| Route | `presetId` | Context |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `/social-media-posting-api` | `api-posting-hub` | — |
| `/social-media-scheduling-api` | `api-scheduling-hub` | — |
| `/social-media-posting-api/{slug}` | `api-posting-platform` | `platformLabel={platformVm.platformLabel}` |
| `/social-media-scheduling-api/{slug}` | `api-scheduling-platform` | `platformLabel={platformVm.platformLabel}` |
| `/` (home) | `home` | optional `cmsSection` from `landingPageConfigVm` (CMS wins over preset defaults) |

**Copy + tab headline overrides:** `web/src/lib/billing/constants/publicPricingLandingSectionConfig.ts` — section subtitle/title/description presets and per-tier `tabHeadline` overrides for landing tabs (`getPublicPricingLandingSection`, `getPublicPricingLandingPlanOverrides`). Dollar amounts and limits stay in `openquok-common`; shared feature bullets and `/pricing` compare rows stay in `publicPricingCatalog.ts`. Re-exported from `$lib/billing` and `$lib/content/constants/apis`.

**Schema.org:** visible section uses `id="pricing"` on `PublicPricingTabs`. Page loaders emit `WebPage` at `{canonical}#pricing` with paid tier + self-host `$0` offers via `createPublicPricingSectionSEOSchema` (`createPublicPricingSEOSchema.ts`; self-host copy from `PUBLIC_SELF_HOST_PRICING_FOOTNOTE_CONFIG`). See **web-seo-jsonld** → Pricing offers.

**Do not** duplicate pricing tab wiring in route files — pass `presetId`, `isLoggedIn`, and optional `platformLabel` only.

## Hero CTAs (docs label + glitch buttons)

Public marketing heroes use **`ButtonGlitchBrightness`** for primary/secondary/ghost actions (not plain `Button`). Docs links use the shared label **`The Getting Started Guide`** from `publicLandingHeroCopy.ts` (`PUBLIC_LANDING_GETTING_STARTED_GUIDE_CTA`) — not “View Docs”.

| Hero | Docs href |
| --- | --- |
| `PublicApiMarketingHero` | `/docs/getting-started-for-public-api` |
| `PublicAgentHero` / `PublicMcpHero` | `agentVm.docsPath` / `mcpVm.docsPath` (setup guide for that integration) |

Apply `landingHeroTheme.ctaButtonClass` on non-aurora heroes (`PublicApiMarketingHero`); use `docsCtaButtonClass` for the longer getting-started label (no `max-w-xs`). Aurora heroes (`PublicAgentHero`, `PublicMcpHero`) keep rounded-full ghost styling on the aurora band with `max-w-none whitespace-nowrap` on the docs button.

## Do not

- Duplicate breadcrumb markup inline in `+page.svelte` — keep trails in dedicated `*Breadcrumb.svelte` wrappers.
- Add a second breadcrumb row above the hero section (outside the hero band).
- Introduce new hub segment labels in page files — extend `publicLandingBreadcrumbConfig.ts` (or the relevant hub VM `metaTitle`) instead.
- Skip uppercase styling on the current (non-link) segment.
- Render marketing `heroTitle` as unstyled plain text — use `PublicLandingHeroTitle` + `landingHeroTheme`.

See also: **web-seo-pseo-templates** (section order), **add-agent** (agent/MCP landing wiring), **public-api-surface-sync** (API marketing pages).
